--
-- The 5% rule (src 463-464, 467): partial permanent injury is paid only if its degree is 5% or
-- more. Fork F11: the degree is the sum of the partial items from one accident, not each item
-- on its own; total permanent injury items are outside the rule.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least degree of partial permanent injury paid` MEANS 5%

GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE
      c IS A `The permanent injury claim`
      `left-handed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`benefit A.2, the rate payable, for the accident on` `the date of the accident` `and the assessment` c `, left-handedness` `left-handed` MEANS
    min 1 (`the total part` PLUS `the partial part`)
    WHERE
        `counted` MEANS filter (GIVEN i YIELD NOT (i's `within another claimed item with a larger amount, for the same injury`)) (c's `items`)
        `the total items` MEANS filter (GIVEN i YIELD `a total permanent injury:` (i's `the injury`)) `counted`
        `the partial items` MEANS filter (GIVEN i YIELD NOT (`a total permanent injury:` (i's `the injury`))) `counted`
        `the rate of` i MEANS `the rate for the permanent injury` (i's `the injury`) `, the insured's left-handedness being` `left-handed`
        `the total part` MEANS
            IF   `permanence is established, counting` `the days in 104 weeks` `days from` `the date of the accident` `, for` c
            THEN sum (map `the rate of` `the total items`)
            ELSE 0
        `the partial sum` MEANS sum (map `the rate of` `the partial items`)
        `the partial part` MEANS
            IF       `permanence is established, counting` `the days in 52 weeks` `days from` `the date of the accident` `, for` c
                 AND `the partial sum` AT LEAST `the least degree of partial permanent injury paid`
            THEN `the partial sum`
            ELSE 0

GIVEN a IS AN `An accident`
      s IS A `The policy schedule`
      c IS A `The permanent injury claim`
      `left-handed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`benefit A.2, the permanent injury benefit, for` a `under` s `on the assessment` c `, left-handedness` `left-handed` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `permanent injury limit`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST l  THEN
        l TIMES `benefit A.2, the rate payable, for the accident on` (a's `date of the accident`) `and the assessment` c `, left-handedness` `left-handed`

§§ `B. Temporary injury`

-- B pays an income allowance while the insured is under treatment for a Temporary Injury, for
-- no longer than the time limits in the summary for each Injury and in total in the period: a
-- daily sum on the limit in the contract, either a fixed sum or by monthly Income, whether or
-- not the Injury is later found permanent, within the amount and time chosen. The daily wage is
-- Income (or the insured's latest declaration the Company confirmed) at the time of the
-- accident divided by 30. Nothing is paid while the insured still receives income, wages or
-- business income.
